    "content": {
      "component": "blog_article",
      "title": "40 years of AKU",
      "description": "",
      "date": "Feb 12, 2023",
      "read_time": "3 min read",
      "author": "Ambreen Merchant",
      "isGlobal": true,
      "banner_image": {
        "fieldtype": "asset",
        "_local": "37-Banner.jpg"
      },
      "thumbnail": {
        "fieldtype": "asset"
      },
      "languages": [],
      "show_share": true,
      "show_similar": true,
      "similar_show_header": true,
      "category": "",
      "isFeatured": null,
      "body": [
        {
          "component": "rich_text",
          "content": {
            "type": "doc",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "World Health Organization",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/books/NBK579606/#:~:text=4%29%20is:%20%E2%80%9COne%20ultrasound%2cIn%20the%20context%20of%20a",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " recommends at least one ultrasound scan before 24 weeks of pregnancy for measuring the foetus to know the duration of pregnancy, and for early detection of foetal and pregnancy anomalies enabling the referral of women with at-risk pregnancies for necessary interventions to prevent poor pregnancy outcomes for mother and baby. However, ultrasound scans are not available and/or affordable for those living in resource-limited settings thus posing a challenge in seeking the service. Moreover, clinical expertise and high-quality scanners are not available in rural healthcare centres."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "The "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Inclusive artificial intelligence for accessible medical imaging across resource-limited settings (AIMIX)",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.ub.edu/web/ub/en/recerca_innovacio/recerca_a_la_UB/projectes/fitxa/I/PE003286/equipInvestigador/index.html?",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " project seeks to address the lack of trained healthcare experts and limited ultrasound screening in rural Africa. Coordinated by the University of Barcelona in collaboration with Aga Khan University's Centre of Excellence in Women and Child Health, East Africa (CoEWCH EA), artificial intelligence (AI) will be used to provide affordable ultrasound scans for women living in resource-limited settings, especially those in rural areas. The goal is to achieve this by developing an affordable and accessible AI technology for early and precise scanning that can be used by minimally trained healthcare workers such as midwives and nurses."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Additionally, CoEWCH EA also hosts the prospective data collection of obstetric ultrasound scans for development of artificial intelligence solutions (iMAMA) project which seeks to collect ultrasound imaging data with the Philips Lumify ultrasound device. The acquired data will be used to design and develop AI algorithms to detect the duration of pregnancy, position of the foetus, cardiac activity, placental position, and number of foetuses. This will help improve the detection rate of some abnormal conditions even by non-expert ultrasound users thus granting women in Kilifi County accessible and affordable quality maternal care. The project is funded by Bill and Melinda Gates Foundation and sponsored by Philips India Ltd and Philips Research."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "As the world continues to increasingly develop and implement new technology, AI is a scientific breakthrough that is revolutionising our lives. It is a very promising technology with applications in healthcare. As stated by "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "UN Women",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "link",
                        "attrs": {
                          "href": "https://www.unwomen.org/en/news-stories/in-focus/2023/03/in-focus-international-womens-day",
                          "target": "_self",
                          "linktype": "url",
                          "uuid": null,
                          "anchor": null,
                          "custom": {}
                        }
                      }
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", digital technology is now presenting opportunities to eliminate all forms of disparity and inequality for the global empowerment of women and girls. Integrative and inclusive AI solutions for affordable ultrasounds will bridge the gap between maternal care in high income countries and in low-and-middle-income countries."
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "paragraph",
                "content": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Conclusively, AI-driven ultrasound scans carry the promise of providing low-cost yet high-quality maternal care to pregnant women in low-resource settings. Achieving this objective will play a crucial part in empowering women and creating a safer space using digital technology. It will equally play a role in closing the gender gap in digital access which prevents women from unlocking technology's full potential. As we mark International Women's Day, we know AI will aid in creating an equal digital future in accordance with this year's theme, "
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "DigitALL: Innovation and technology for gender equality.",
                    "marks": [
                      {
                        "type": "bold"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
